  "question": {
    "text": "The modulus of $\\frac{1-i}{3+i}+\\frac{4 i}{5}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PGK0O",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{5}$ unit",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ep88i",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{5}$ unit",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "36Out",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}$ unit",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "RZsVN",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{12}}{5}$ unit",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\text { Hints: } \\frac{1-i}{3+i}+\\frac{4 i}{5}=\\frac{5-5 i+4 i(3+i)}{5(3+i)}=\\frac{5-5 i+12 i-4}{5(3+i)}=\\frac{1+7 i}{5(3+i)}=\\frac{(1+7 i)(3-i)}{5(9+1)}\n$$\n\n$$\n=\\frac{3+21 i-i+7}{5 \\times 10}=\\frac{10+20 i}{5 \\times 10}=\\frac{1+2 i}{5}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\therefore \\text { Modulus }=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{25}+\\frac{4}{25}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\text { unit }\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
